"""One currency, honest annual income, and a builder that replaces.

Portfolio totals added Canadian and US dollars together, so a US holding was
overstated by the exchange rate and the builder bought about 1.4x too many of
its shares. A fund younger than a year had a few months of payments presented
as a year of income. And "Use this portfolio" inserted on top of whatever was
already saved, so using it twice doubled the portfolio.
"""
